{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550434541,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","part":{"partID":"prt_1d38a8615001sQPMSayi1grQ9K","sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","messageID":"msg_1d38a5ae0001sJHVTmB0L8WMD9","type":"tool","id":"call_d8cebcd3029b4e88924ad9de","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"holdout\\|Holdout\\|HOLDOUT\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/worktree-restore.mjs .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md | head -80"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:912:// is joined to its row before a transcript is read. A holdout row is marked and\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:933:    holdout: false,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:948:    labels.set(row.id, row.split === 'holdout' ? { holdout: true } : rowLabel(row));\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:960:    holdout: false,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1157:  if (label.holdout) return { scored: false, reason: 'holdout_row' };\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:578:// A row is read one line at a time so a holdout row is refused before its prompt\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:588:    if (row.split === 'holdout') {\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:589:      throw new Refusal('holdout_row', `${rowId}: a holdout row is never run`);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:331:    byFamily.set(namespace, { tune: emptyAttachedTally(), holdout: emptyAttachedTally() });\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:446:      perCommand.set(command, { typed: emptyTally(), plain: { tune: emptyTally(), holdout: emptyTally() } });\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:450:    const plain = { tune: emptyTally(), holdout: emptyTally() };\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:473:    const plainAttached = { tune: emptyAttachedTally(), holdout: emptyAttachedTally() };\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:494:      const isPlainSplit = row.row_type === 'plain' && (row.split === 'tune' || row.split === 'holdout');\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:594:        holdout: attachedTallyJson(family.holdout),\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:609:          holdout: { correct: plain.holdout.top1, total: plain.holdout.rows },\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:613:          holdout: { correct: plain.holdout.top3, total: plain.holdout.rows },\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:630:          holdout: attachedTallyJson(plainAttached.holdout),\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:78:- `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when the corpus refuses a row id, because every prompt is resolved before the first line is written and a refused row leaves no output file behind.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:97:- Flags: `node measure-brief-cost.mjs [--rows <id,id>] [--root <dir>]` keeps every typed row on the `none` split, `--rows` narrows the run to named corpus ids and `--root` names the checkout the corpus and hook are read from, defaulting to the current directory. A holdout or unknown id exits 2 before anything is spawned, and no prompt is ever printed.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:112:| `command-offer.mjs` | Recovers the attribution fields for a run line. `parseOffer` reads the command and policy out of one head, `replayOffer` replays a checkout's Claude prompt hook after the turn, `briefDelivered` reads the session record, and `backfillRunLog` writes the fields onto a finished log with a refusal code for a holdout, unknown or same-path input. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:113:| `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. `--backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]` rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` instead of running a turn, and prints a JSON refusal with `same_path`, `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when it cannot. After each turn it restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths` whose status still differs from the snapshot taken before the turn. Exit 2 refuses instead of running: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout or unknown row, a set with fewer rows than it needs (`set_short`), a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder (`worktree_dirty`), a checkout with a git remote (`remote_present`), or a Codex arm whose project hook is unapproved (`codex-hooks-unapproved`). |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:154:Exit 2 means the run was refused before or during its first prompt: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout row, a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder, or a checkout that still has a git remote.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:163:The output log holds the same lines plus `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offerError`, `briefDelivered` and `offerBackfilled`. Exit 2 means the output was refused, and the printed JSON names why: `same_path`, `holdout_row`, `unknown_row` or a missing `--out`.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:912:// is joined to its row before a transcript is read. A holdout row is marked and\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:933:    holdout: false,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:948:    labels.set(row.id, row.split === 'holdout' ? { holdout: true } : rowLabel(row));\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:960:    holdout: false,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1157:  if (label.holdout) return { scored: false, reason: 'holdout_row' };\n.skilled/