{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550617643,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","part":{"partID":"prt_1d38d53ae001kgMZyk6JtQw7Lu","sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","messageID":"msg_1d38d216e0014nX7mGRXXwdJjF","type":"tool","id":"call_ba39876785c745acac9a88e1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":220,"offset":740,"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs, lines 740-959\n740: // A placeholder keeps the fixed prompts free of a path that only exists on the\n741: // machine the arm runs on.\n742: function promptFor(rowId, fixture) {\n743:   const fixed = G2_PROMPTS.get(rowId);\n744:   if (fixed === undefined) return lookupPrompt(rowId).prompt;\n745:   return fixed.split(FIXTURE_TOKEN).join(fixture);\n746: }\n747: \n748: // The cap belongs to the prompt rather than to the invocation, so an arm that\n749: // mixes the two sets still gives a started workflow the time it needs.\n750: function capForRow(rowId) {\n751:   return G2_PROMPTS.has(rowId) ? CAP_MS.started : CAP_MS.chat;\n752: }\n753: \n754: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n755: // One turn\n756: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n757: \n758: // A dispatched worker's marker makes a CLI answer as a child session, and a child\n759: // session is not the chat start an arm measures. The rest of the environment stays,\n760: // so each CLI finds its own home, account and route.\n761: //\n762: // The network credentials are the exception, because a turn that reaches a forge\n763: // with the operator's identity is a side effect no transcript can undo. The token\n764: // variables go, the GitHub CLI is pointed at an empty folder beside the run log\n765: // rather than the operator's authenticated one, and an empty credential helper\n766: // replaces whatever a global git config would have offered. A missing credential\n767: // then fails at once instead of waiting on a terminal nobody is sitting at.\n768: const GITHUB_TOKEN_VARS = Object.freeze(['GH_TOKEN', 'GITHUB_TOKEN', 'GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN']);\n769: \n770: const GIT_CREDENTIAL_OVERRIDES = Object.freeze({\n771:   GIT_CONFIG_COUNT: '1',\n772:   GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0: 'credential.helper',\n773:   GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0: '',\n774: });\n775: \n776: // The empty folder lives beside the run log, so a run leaves its own directory\n777: // behind instead of a path in the operator's home that the next run inherits.\n778: function ghConfigDir(outPath) {\n779:   return join(dirname(outPath), 'gh-config-empty');\n780: }\n781: \n782: function childEnv(ghConfig) {\n783:   const env = { ...process.env };\n784:   delete env.AI_SESSION_CHILD;\n785:   for (const name of GITHUB_TOKEN_VARS) delete env[name];\n786:   env.GH_CONFIG_DIR = ghConfig;\n787:   env.GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT = '0';\n788:   Object.assign(env, GIT_CREDENTIAL_OVERRIDES);\n789:   return env;\n790: }\n791: \n792: function spawnTurn(runtime, argv, prompt, capMs, ghConfig) {\n793:   return new Promise((settle) => {\n794:     // A CLI that reads the prompt from stdin gets a pipe to write it into. Every other\n795:     // runtime keeps stdin ignored, because an open stdin leaves that CLI waiting on\n796:     // input nobody types until the cap runs out into an empty transcript.\n797:     const child = spawn(runtime.command, argv, {\n798:       cwd: REPO_ROOT,\n799:       env: childEnv(ghConfig),\n800:       // Ignored means the child reads /dev/null rather than blocking on a terminal.\n801:       stdio: [runtime.promptOnStdin ? 'pipe' : 'ignore', 'pipe', 'inherit'],\n802:       // A chat turn still running after its cap is stuck, while a started workflow\n803:       // legitimately needs the longer one. The prompt decides which it gets.\n804:       timeout: capMs,\n805:     });\n806:     // The prompt is written and the stream closed at once, so a CLI that reads until\n807:     // the end of input sees a whole prompt. A CLI that exits before reading leaves a\n808:     // broken pipe behind, and that write error is the CLI's failure to report rather\n809:     // than an uncaught error that would end the run early.\n810:     if (child.stdin !== null) {\n811:       child.stdin.on('error', () => {});\n812:       child.stdin.end(prompt);\n813:     }\n814:     const locator = streamLocator(runtime.locator.field ?? null);\n815:     // The turn's own output is still shown, and the locator is read out of the\n816:     // same bytes, so watching a run and recording it never diverge.\n817:     child.stdout.setEncoding('utf8');\n818:     child.stdout.on('data', (chunk) => {\n819:       locator.push(chunk);\n820:       process.stdout.write(chunk);\n821:     });\n822:     child.on('error', (error) => settle({ exit: null, error, streamId: null }));\n823:     child.on('close', (exit) => settle({ exit, error: null, streamId: locator.value() }));\n824:   });\n825: }\n826: \n827: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n828: // CLI\n829: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n830: \n831: class UsageError extends Error {}\n832: \n833: const SCRIPT_NAME = 'run-command-behaviour.mjs';\n834: const SAMPLE_PROMPT = 'sample prompt for argv inspection';\n835: const SAMPLE_SESSION_ID = 'sample-session-id';\n836: \n837: // An arm label decides how a later scorer groups a whole log, so a typo would\n838: // quietly invent a third arm. The set is closed for that reason.\n839: const ARMS = ['pre', 'post', 'smoke', 'g2'];\n840: \n841: // The pre-change arm is the default because it is the one that can run before the\n842: // brief lands. A post-change run has to say which arm it belongs to. The\n843: // started-command set carries its own arm, so a run of it cannot land in the\n844: // change comparison by omission.\n845: const DEFAULT_ARM = 'pre';\n846: \n847: const USAGE = [\n848:   `usage: ${SCRIPT_NAME} --print-argv <runtime>`,\n849:   `       ${SCRIPT_NAME} --list <set>`,\n850:   `       ${SCRIPT_NAME} --runtime <runtime> (--set <set> | --row-id <id>...)`,\n851:   '         --out <run-log> [--arm <arm>] [--fixture <dir>] [--dry-run]',\n852:   `       ${SCRIPT_NAME} --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]`,\n853: ].join('\\n');\n854: \n855: function resolveRuntime(name) {\n856:   if (has(RUNTIMES, name)) {\n857:     return RUNTIMES[name];\n858:   }\n859:   if (has(NOT_MEASURED, name)) {\n860:     throw new UsageError(`runtime ${name} is not measured: ${NOT_MEASURED[name]}`);\n861:   }\n862:   throw new UsageError(`unknown runtime: ${name}`);\n863: }\n864: \n865: function valueAfter(argv, index, flag) {\n866:   const value = argv[index];\n867:   if (typeof value !== 'string' || value.startsWith('--')) {\n868:     throw new UsageError(`${flag}: a value is required`);\n869:   }\n870:   return value;\n871: }\n872: \n873: // A set that has its own arm names it, so a started-command run cannot join the\n874: // change comparison because nobody passed `--arm`.\n875: function armFor(options) {\n876:   if (options.arm !== null) return options.arm;\n877:   return options.set === G2_SET ? G2_SET : DEFAULT_ARM;\n878: }\n879: \n880: function parseOptions(argv) {\n881:   const options = {\n882:     printArgv: null,\n883:     list: null,\n884:     set: null,\n885:     runtime: null,\n886:     rowIds: [],\n887:     arm: null,\n888:     out: null,\n889:     backfill: null,\n890:     fixture: null,\n891:     dryRun: false,\n892:     briefOnly: false,\n893:   };\n894:   for (let index = 0; index < argv.length; index += 1) {\n895:     const token = argv[index];\n896:     if (token === '--print-argv') {\n897:       index += 1;\n898:       options.printArgv = valueAfter(argv, index, '--print-argv');\n899:     } else if (token === '--list') {\n900:       index += 1;\n901:       options.list = valueAfter(argv, index, '--list');\n902:     } else if (token === '--set') {\n903:       index += 1;\n904:       options.set = valueAfter(argv, index, '--set');\n905:     } else if (token === '--runtime') {\n906:       index += 1;\n907:       options.runtime = valueAfter(argv, index, '--runtime');\n908:     } else if (token === '--row-id') {\n909:       index += 1;\n910:       options.rowIds.push(valueAfter(argv, index, '--row-id'));\n911:     } else if (token === '--arm') {\n912:       index += 1;\n913:       const arm = valueAfter(argv, index, '--arm');\n914:       if (!ARMS.includes(arm)) {\n915:         throw new UsageError(`--arm: expected one of ${ARMS.join(', ')}`);\n916:       }\n917:       options.arm = arm;\n918:     } else if (token === '--out') {\n919:       index += 1;\n920:       options.out = resolve(valueAfter(argv, index, '--out'));\n921:     } else if (token === '--backfill') {\n922:       index += 1;\n923:       options.backfill = resolve(valueAfter(argv, index, '--backfill'));\n924:     } else if (token === '--fixture') {\n925:       index += 1;\n926:       options.fixture = resolve(valueAfter(argv, index, '--fixture'));\n927:     } else if (token === '--dry-run') {\n928:       options.dryRun = true;\n929:     } else if (token === '--brief-only') {\n930:       options.briefOnly = true;\n931:     } else {\n932:       throw new UsageError(`unknown option: ${token}`);\n933:     }\n934:   }\n935:   return options;\n936: }\n937: \n938: // One mode per invocation. Asking for an argv and a run at once would hide which\n939: // one the operator meant, and a run with no log has nowhere to record its proof.\n940: function selectMode(options) {\n941:   // Only a backfill rewrites delivery, so the flag on any other invocation would\n942:   // parse and then quietly change nothing.\n943:   if (options.briefOnly && options.backfill === null) {\n944:     throw new UsageError('--brief-only needs --backfill');\n945:   }\n946:   if (options.printArgv !== null) return 'print-argv';\n947:   if (options.list !== null) return 'list';\n948:   if (options.backfill !== null) {\n949:     if (options.out === null) throw new UsageError('--out is required');\n950:     return 'backfill';\n951:   }\n952:   if (options.runtime === null) throw new UsageError('--runtime is required');\n953:   if (options.set === null && options.rowIds.length === 0) {\n954:     throw new UsageError('--set or --row-id is required');\n955:   }\n956:   if (options.out === null) throw new UsageError('--out is required');\n957:   return 'run';\n958: }\n959: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 960]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs, lines 740-959\n740: // A placeholder keeps the fixed prompts free of a path that only exists on the\n741: // machine the arm runs on.\n742: function promptFor(rowId, fixture) {\n743:   const fixed = G2_PROMPTS.get(rowId);\n744:   if (fixed === undefined) return lookupPrompt(rowId).prompt;\n745:   return fixed.split(FIXTURE_TOKEN).join(fixture);\n746: }\n747: \n748: // The cap belongs to the prompt rather than to the invocation, so an arm that\n749: // mixes the two sets still gives a started workflow the time it needs.\n750: function capForRow(rowId) {\n751:   return G2_PROMPTS.has(rowId) ? CAP_MS.started : CAP_MS.chat;\n752: }\n753: \n754: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n755: // One turn\n756: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n757: \n758: // A dispatched worker's marker makes a CLI answer as a child session, and a child\n759: // session is not the chat start an arm measures. The rest of the environment stays,\n760: // so each CLI finds its own home, account and route.\n761: //\n762: // The network credentials are the exception, because a turn that reaches a forge\n763: // with the operator's identity is a side effect