{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551208629,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","part":{"partID":"prt_1d396587b001b5LwgSD7syBge0","sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","messageID":"msg_1d3963dfa001VSeyJ1N1ChJbUP","type":"tool","id":"call_4d3c4605ff4d4d83b3c9ddb0","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":65,"offset":58,"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 58-122\n58: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n59: - Reading the invariant at both ends (holdout guard in scorer/runner vs. report publication in baseline) surfaced a leak a single-file read would miss (iteration 1).\n60: - Counting corpus splits through `split`/`row_type` tallies instead of prompt text kept the review holdout-safe while still proving composition (iteration 1).\n61: - Checking every renderer head shape against `BRIEF_PATTERN` eliminated a suspected false-negative instead of reporting it (iteration 1).\n62: \n63: ---\n64: \n65: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n66: - An early suspicion that the README named a non-existent Python file was wrong; the file exists, so the finding was narrowed to the real inventory drift (iteration 1).\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n71: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n72: ### `--dry-run` is not side-effect free: it still replays the Claude hook (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:1043-1047`), which spawns a process. Ruled out as a finding because the code comments state the replay explicitly and no documentation claims a dry run spawns nothing; recorded as a behavior note only. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n73: - What was tried: `--dry-run` is not side-effect free: it still replays the Claude hook (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:1043-1047`), which spawns a process. Ruled out as a finding because the code comments state the replay explicitly and no documentation claims a dry run spawns nothing; recorded as a behavior note only.\n74: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n75: - Do NOT retry: `--dry-run` is not side-effect free: it still replays the Claude hook (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:1043-1047`), which spawns a process. Ruled out as a finding because the code comments state the replay explicitly and no documentation claims a dry run spawns nothing; recorded as a behavior note only.\n76: \n77: ### Claude/codex/pi/devin/dsh brief detection false negatives: every renderer head shape and every reader branch was checked against `render.ts:581-638`; no mismatch found. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n78: - What was tried: Claude/codex/pi/devin/dsh brief detection false negatives: every renderer head shape and every reader branch was checked against `render.ts:581-638`; no mismatch found.\n79: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n80: - Do NOT retry: Claude/codex/pi/devin/dsh brief detection false negatives: every renderer head shape and every reader branch was checked against `render.ts:581-638`; no mismatch found.\n81: \n82: ### Staged-new-file restoration: `restorePath` drops the index entry and deletes the file, covering the case a restore-from-index would miss (`worktree-restore.mjs:61-84`). No finding. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n83: - What was tried: Staged-new-file restoration: `restorePath` drops the index entry and deletes the file, covering the case a restore-from-index would miss (`worktree-restore.mjs:61-84`). No finding.\n84: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n85: - Do NOT retry: Staged-new-file restoration: `restorePath` drops the index entry and deletes the file, covering the case a restore-from-index would miss (`worktree-restore.mjs:61-84`). No finding.\n86: \n87: ### Untracked-directory collapse in `git status --porcelain`: considered as a restore gap, but the runner refuses a dirty worktree outside the run-log folder before the first live turn (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:994-1000`), so a pre-existing untracked directory cannot silently absorb turn writes in the measured arms. Not promoted without a reachable case. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n88: - What was tried: Untracked-directory collapse in `git status --porcelain`: considered as a restore gap, but the runner refuses a dirty worktree outside the run-log folder before the first live turn (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:994-1000`), so a pre-existing untracked directory cannot silently absorb turn writes in the measured arms. Not promoted without a reachable case.\n89: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n90: - Do NOT retry: Untracked-directory collapse in `git status --porcelain`: considered as a restore gap, but the runner refuses a dirty worktree outside the run-log folder before the first live turn (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:994-1000`), so a pre-existing untracked directory cannot silently absorb turn writes in the measured arms. Not promoted without a reachable case.\n91: \n92: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n93: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n94: - Completed pivots: 0\n95: - Failed pivots: 0\n96: - Audited overrides: 0\n97: - Swept: none yet\n98: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n99: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n100: \n101: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n102: - `--dry-run` spawn-free claim: the replay is explicit in code comments and no doc claims otherwise; behavior note only (iteration 1, evidence: `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1043-1047`).\n103: - Staged-new-file restore gap: `restorePath` drops the index entry and deletes the file (iteration 1, evidence: `worktree-restore.mjs:61-84`).\n104: - Untracked-directory collapse as a silent restore gap: the pre-turn dirty guard makes it unreachable in measured arms (iteration 1, evidence: `run-command-behaviour.mjs:994-1000`).\n105: - Brief-detection false negatives across claude/codex/pi/devin/dsh: every head shape matches `BRIEF_PATTERN` (iteration 1, evidence: `render.ts:581-638`).\n106: \n107: ---\n108: \n109: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n110: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n111: - Dimension: security - Focus area: safety of offering a mutating command in the live-turn harness and arena (remote/dirty/worktree guards, credential scrubbing, restore completeness, fixture trust), plus secrets exposure in measured environments. - Reason: iteration 1 confirmed the read paths are holdout-safe but exposed a report-path leak; the highest remaining risk in the review focus is a measured turn that writes outside its arena or reaches the network with operator credentials. - Rotation status: D1 correctness complete, D2 security next. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (source-level guard audit); blocked (cannot execute turns under containment). - Required evidence: exact guard lines in `run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, `worktree-restore.mjs`, and the playbook chapter that instructs operators how to run a live arm. Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n112: \n113: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n114: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n115: \n116: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n117: \n118: - Target pointers: 29 `accuracy-runner` files from `review-scope.txt` (routing-accuracy runners/corpora, cost benches, transcript/offer tests, legacy fidelity tests, manual-testing playbook). Shared docs: `system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `runtime/scripts/README.md`, `runtime/tests/README.md`, `feature-catalog/*`, `sk-doc` docs.\n119: - Behavior claims to verify: routed command surfacing must be cross-runtime correct (claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh); a mutating command must never be offered unsafely (no implicit `:auto` invocation of a writing workflow); holdout rows must never be read by tune/fix/report paths; documentation must match runner behavior.\n120: - Reuse and conventions: append-gateway state recording, `validate.sh --strict` evidence discipline, P0/P1/P2 severity ladder, three-artifact iteration contract.\n121: - Review risks and gaps: holdout prompt text is out of read scope (counts only); fan-out containment forbids running repo tooling that writes outside the lineage, so runners are audited by reading, not by execution; coverage graph seed skipped by containment (see edge cases).\n122: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 123]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 58-122\n58: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n59: - Reading the invariant at both ends (holdout guard in scorer/runner vs. report publication in baseline) surfaced a leak a single-file read would miss (iteration 1).\n60: - Counting corpus splits through `split`/`row_type` tallies instead of prompt text kept the review holdout-safe while still proving composition (iteration 1).\n61: - Checking every renderer head shape against `BRIEF_PATTERN` eliminated a suspected false-negative instead of reporting it (iteration 1).\n62: \n63: ---\n64: \n65: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n66: - An early suspicion that the README named a non-existent Python file was wrong; the file exists, so the finding was narrowed to the real inventory drift (iteration 1).\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n71: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n72: ### `--dry-run` is not side-effect free: it still replays the Claude hook (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:1043-1047`), which spawns a process. Ruled out as a finding because the code comments state the replay explicitly and no documentation claims a dry run spawns nothing; recorded as a behavior note only. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n73: - What was tried: `--dry-run` is not side-effec