{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551230458,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","part":{"partID":"prt_1d39682440022CdE2d0Bag8LYB","sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","messageID":"msg_1d39664e4001JKGtQ0SujGbMFU","type":"tool","id":"call_19d9722241474873aa6198fb","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Reading the invariant at both ends (holdout guard in scorer/runner vs. report publication in baseline) surfaced a leak a single-file read would miss (iteration 1).\n- Counting corpus splits through `split`/`row_type` tallies instead of prompt text kept the review holdout-safe while still proving composition (iteration 1).\n- Checking every renderer head shape against `BRIEF_PATTERN` eliminated a suspected false-negative instead of reporting it (iteration 1).\n- Building a per-runtime permission matrix from the six `buildArgv` entries turned \"the arena contains it\" into a checkable claim and exposed which runtimes have no OS-level bound (iteration 2).\n- Comparing the header threat model against `childEnv` caught an overclaim that no single function read would show (iteration 2).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- An early suspicion that the README named a non-existent Python file was wrong; the file exists, so the finding was narrowed to the real inventory drift (iteration 1).\n- Trying to promote the \"no arena assertion\" gap to P1 failed the reach test: the documented operator path runs from the arena clone, whose empty remote list satisfies the guard, so it stays P2 hardening (iteration 2).","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Reading the invariant at both ends (holdout guard in scorer/runner vs. report publication in baseline) surfaced a leak a single-file read would miss (iteration 1).\n- Counting corpus splits through `split`/`row_type` tallies instead of prompt text kept the review holdout-safe while still proving composition (iteration 1).\n- Checking every renderer head shape against `BRIEF_PATTERN` eliminated a suspected false-negative instead of reporting it (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- An early suspicion that the README named a non-existent Python file was wrong; the file exists, so the finding was narrowed to the real inventory drift (iteration 1).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -58,13 +58,16 @@\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n - Reading the invariant at both ends (holdout guard in scorer/runner vs. report publication in baseline) surfaced a leak a single-file read would miss (iteration 1).\n - Counting corpus splits through `split`/`row_type` tallies instead of prompt text kept the review holdout-safe while still proving composition (iteration 1).\n - Checking every renderer head shape against `BRIEF_PATTERN` eliminated a suspected false-negative instead of reporting it (iteration 1).\n+- Building a per-runtime permission matrix from the six `buildArgv` entries turned \"the arena contains it\" into a checkable claim and exposed which runtimes have no OS-level bound (iteration 2).\n+- Comparing the header threat model against `childEnv` caught an overclaim that no single function read would show (iteration 2).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n - An early suspicion that the README named a non-existent Python file was wrong; the file exists, so the finding was narrowed to the real inventory drift (iteration 1).\n+- Trying to promote the \"no arena assertion\" gap to P1 failed the reach test: the documented operator path runs from the arena clone, whose empty remote list satisfies the guard, so it stays P2 hardening (iteration 2).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n- Reading the invariant at both ends (holdout guard in scorer/runner vs. report publication in baseline) surfaced a leak a single-file read would miss (iteration 1).\\n- Counting corpus splits through `split`/`row_type` tallies instead of prompt text kept the review holdout-safe while still proving composition (iteration 1).\\n- Checking every renderer head shape against `BRIEF_PATTERN` eliminated a suspected false-negative instead of reporting it (iteration 1).\\n- Building a per-runtime permission matrix from the six `buildArgv` entries turned \\\"the arena contains it\\\" into a checkable claim and exposed which runtimes have no OS-level bound (iteration 2).\\n- Comparing the header threat model against `childEnv` caught an overclaim that no single function read would show (iteration 2).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n- An early suspicion that the README named a non-existent Python file was wrong; the file exists, so the finding was narrowed to the real inventory drift (iteration 1).\\n- Trying to promote the \\\"no arena assertion\\\" gap to P1 failed the reach test: the documented operator path runs from the arena clone, whose empty remote list satisfies the guard, so it stays P2 hardening (iteration 2).\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n- Reading the invariant at both ends (holdout guard in scorer/runner vs. report publication in baseline) surfaced a leak a single-file read would miss (iteration 1).\\n- Counting corpus splits through `split`/`row_type` tallies instead of prompt text kept the review holdout-safe while still proving composition (iteration 1).\\n- Checking every renderer head shape against `BRIEF_PATTERN` eliminated a suspected false-negative instead of reporting it (iteration 1).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n- An early suspicion that the README named a non-existent Python file was wrong; the file exists, so the finding was narrowed to the real inventory drift (iteration 1).\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551218756,"end":1794551230458}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551230467,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","part":{"partID":"prt_1d3969730001fsA8QpPbmHzbrG","sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","messageID":"msg_1d39664e4001JKGtQ0SujGbMFU","type":"tool","id":"call_d667844ef8f1485ba1a82460","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 2\n- Failed pivots: 1\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: holdout guard in scoring/runner paths; offer parsing against all shipped command shapes; renderer heads vs BRIEF_PATTERN; six-runtime permission matrix; environment builder\n- Pivot lineage: D1 correctness (iteration 1) -> D2 security (iteration 2) -> D3 traceability (iteration 3)\n- Remaining frontier: D3 traceability, D4 maintainability; live-turn execution evidence blocked by containment\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n- `--dry-run` spawn-free claim: the replay is explicit in code comments and no doc claims otherwise; behavior note only (iteration 1, evidence: `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1043-1047`).\n- Staged-new-file restore gap: `restorePath` drops the index entry and deletes the file (iteration 1, evidence: `worktree-restore.mjs:61-84`).\n- Untracked-directory collapse as a silent restore gap: the pre-turn dirty guard makes it unreachable in measured arms (iteration 1, evidence: `run-command-behaviour.mjs:994-1000`).\n- Brief-detection false negatives across claude/codex/pi/devin/dsh: every head shape matches `BRIEF_PATTERN` (iteration 1, evidence: `render.ts:581-638`).\n- OpenCode `--auto` as a standalone finding: required to observe an ask row and covered by the arena model; folded into the environment finding (iteration 2, evidence: `run-command-behaviour.mjs:176-178`).\n- Prompt leakage through argv: corpus prompts are not secret and holdout ids are refused before a prompt reaches argv (iteration 2, evidence: `run-command-behaviour.mjs:583-594,724-727`).","oldString":"## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n- `--dry-run` spawn-free claim: the replay is explicit in code comments and no doc claims otherwise; behavior note only (iteration 1, evidence: `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1043-1047`).\n- Staged-new-file restore gap: `restorePath` drops the index entry and deletes the file (iteration 1, evidence: `worktree-restore.mjs:61-84`).\n- Untracked-directory collapse as a silent restore gap: the pre-turn dirty guard makes it unreachable in measured arms (iteration 1, evidence: `run-command-behaviour.mjs:994-1000`).\n- Brief-detection false negatives across claude/codex/pi/devin/dsh: every head shape matches `BRIEF_PATTERN` (iteration 1, evidence: `render.ts:581-638`).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -93,20 +93,22 @@\n - Do NOT retry: Untracked-directory collapse in `git status --porcelain`: considered as a restore gap, but the runner refuses a dirty worktree outside the run-log folder before the first live turn (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:994-1000`), so a pre-existing untracked directory cannot silently absorb turn writes in the measured arms. Not promoted without a reachable case.\n \n <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n-- Completed pivots: 0\n-- Failed pivots: 0\n+- Completed pivots: 2\n+- Failed pivots: 1\n - Audited overrides: 0\n-- Swept: none yet\n-- Pivot lineage: none yet\n-- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n+- Swept: holdout guard in scoring/runner paths; offer parsing against all shipped command shapes; renderer heads vs BRIEF_PATTERN; six-runtime permission matrix; environment builder\n+- Pivot lineage: D1 correctness (iteration 1) -> D2 security (iteration 2) -> D3 traceability (iteration 3)\n+- Remaining frontier: D3 traceability, D4 maintainability; live-turn execution evidence blocked by containment\n \n ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n - `--dry-run` spawn-free claim: the replay is explicit in code comments and no doc claims otherwise; behavior note only (iteration 1, evidence: `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1043-1047`).\n - Staged-new-file restore gap: `restorePath` drops the index entry and deletes the file (iteration 1, evidence: `worktree-restore.mjs:61-84`).\n - Untracked-directory collapse as a silent restore gap: the pre-turn dirty guard makes it unreachable in measured arms (iteration 1, evidence: `run-command-behaviour.mjs:994-1000`).\n - Brief-detection false negatives across claude/codex/pi/devin/dsh: every head shape matches `BRIEF_PATTERN` (iteration 1, evidence: `render.ts:581-638`).\n+- OpenCode `--auto` as a standalone finding: required to observe an ask row and covered by the arena model; folded into the environment finding (iteration 2, evidence: `run-command-behaviour.mjs:176-178`).\n+- Prompt leakage through argv: corpus prompts are not secret and holdout ids are refused before a 