{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551244862,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","part":{"partID":"prt_1d396c901001veREWcDHJMKQpN","sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","messageID":"msg_1d396b6f7001vzXkD03NMNxIVb","type":"tool","id":"call_0c848b1046e447d6a01a708b","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: traceability\n- Focus area: packet/playbook claims versus harness behavior (arena precondition, exit codes 2/3, offerReached semantics, holdout split treatment, README inventory), plus the tests that pin them.\n- Reason: the security posture is established; the remaining review-focus value is whether an operator following the documented path reaches the safe path, and whether tests hold the documented behavior.\n- Rotation status: D2 security complete; D3 traceability next.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (runtime table + environment builder); blocked (no live execution evidence).\n- Required evidence: manual-testing-playbook.md, native-cli-tools/hub-command-attachment.md, runtime/tests/README.md, command-offer.vitest.ts, command-transcript-score.vitest.ts, packet capability claims.\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->","oldString":"<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: security - Focus area: safety of offering a mutating command in the live-turn harness and arena (remote/dirty/worktree guards, credential scrubbing, restore completeness, fixture trust), plus secrets exposure in measured environments. - Reason: iteration 1 confirmed the read paths are holdout-safe but exposed a report-path leak; the highest remaining risk in the review focus is a measured turn that writes outside its arena or reaches the network with operator credentials. - Rotation status: D1 correctness complete, D2 security next. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (source-level guard audit); blocked (cannot execute turns under containment). - Required evidence: exact guard lines in `run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, `worktree-restore.mjs`, and the playbook chapter that instructs operators how to run a live arm. Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -112,9 +112,14 @@\n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-- Dimension: security - Focus area: safety of offering a mutating command in the live-turn harness and arena (remote/dirty/worktree guards, credential scrubbing, restore completeness, fixture trust), plus secrets exposure in measured environments. - Reason: iteration 1 confirmed the read paths are holdout-safe but exposed a report-path leak; the highest remaining risk in the review focus is a measured turn that writes outside its arena or reaches the network with operator credentials. - Rotation status: D1 correctness complete, D2 security next. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (source-level guard audit); blocked (cannot execute turns under containment). - Required evidence: exact guard lines in `run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, `worktree-restore.mjs`, and the playbook chapter that instructs operators how to run a live arm. Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n+- Dimension: traceability\n+- Focus area: packet/playbook claims versus harness behavior (arena precondition, exit codes 2/3, offerReached semantics, holdout split treatment, README inventory), plus the tests that pin them.\n+- Reason: the security posture is established; the remaining review-focus value is whether an operator following the documented path reaches the safe path, and whether tests hold the documented behavior.\n+- Rotation status: D2 security complete; D3 traceability next.\n+- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (runtime table + environment builder); blocked (no live execution evidence).\n+- Required evidence: manual-testing-playbook.md, native-cli-tools/hub-command-attachment.md, runtime/tests/README.md, command-offer.vitest.ts, command-transcript-score.vitest.ts, packet capability claims.\n \n <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n \n","status":"modified","additions":6,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\n- Dimension: traceability\\n- Focus area: packet/playbook claims versus harness behavior (arena precondition, exit codes 2/3, offerReached semantics, holdout split treatment, README inventory), plus the tests that pin them.\\n- Reason: the security posture is established; the remaining review-focus value is whether an operator following the documented path reaches the safe path, and whether tests hold the documented behavior.\\n- Rotation status: D2 security complete; D3 traceability next.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (runtime table + environment builder); blocked (no live execution evidence).\\n- Required evidence: manual-testing-playbook.md, native-cli-tools/hub-command-attachment.md, runtime/tests/README.md, command-offer.vitest.ts, command-transcript-score.vitest.ts, packet capability claims.\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\",\"oldString\":\"<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\n- Dimension: security - Focus area: safety of offering a mutating command in the live-turn harness and arena (remote/dirty/worktree guards, credential scrubbing, restore completeness, fixture trust), plus secrets exposure in measured environments. - Reason: iteration 1 confirmed the read paths are holdout-safe but exposed a report-path leak; the highest remaining risk in the review focus is a measured turn that writes outside its arena or reaches the network with operator credentials. - Rotation status: D1 correctness complete, D2 security next. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (source-level guard audit); blocked (cannot execute turns under containment). - Required evidence: exact guard lines in `run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, `worktree-restore.mjs`, and the playbook chapter that instructs operators how to run a live arm. Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551236865,"end":1794551244862}}}}
