{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551309812,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","part":{"partID":"prt_1d397e50b001Tn5PXQn9sR8Cas","sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","messageID":"msg_1d397c940001a3OispPFTdmCnl","type":"tool","id":"call_de700eca2fef488487d3d1ce","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/hub-command-attachment.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/hub-command-attachment.md, lines 1-124\n1: ---\n2: title: \"NC-011 Hub Recommendation Names Its Slash Command\"\n3: description: \"Manual validation that advisor_recommend adds the routed mode's slash command to a hub recommendation, holds a deep-loop command back until the prompt asks for depth and does not report a command row and its owner as a tie.\"\n4: version: 1.0.0.0\n5: id: NC-011\n6: category: native_cli_tools\n7: stage: routing\n8: ---\n9: \n10: # NC-011 Hub Recommendation Names Its Slash Command\n11: \n12: Prompt: Manual validation that advisor_recommend adds the routed mode's slash command to a hub recommendation, holds a deep-loop command back until the prompt asks for depth and does not report a command row and its owner as a tie.\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n17: \n18: A hub skill such as `sk-doc` used to come back as a bare skill id. The reader then had to work out which slash command runs the mode the hub picked. When a hub's compiled route picks exactly one mode, the recommendation now carries a `command` field with that mode's slash command.\n19: \n20: This scenario checks three rules with four real prompts:\n21: \n22: 1. A plain authoring prompt for `sk-doc` returns `command: \"/create:readme\"`.\n23: 2. A `system-deep-loop` command is attached only when the prompt asks for depth. A prompt that names the topic gets the same route and no command.\n24: 3. A command row and the skill that owns it are one answer, so their near tie does not set `ambiguous`.\n25: \n26: ---\n27: \n28: ## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT\n29: \n30: - Objective: Confirm the `command` field on a single-mode hub route, the deep-loop effort gate and the same-owner tie rule.\n31: - Real user request: `When the advisor picks sk-doc for my README, does it tell me which command to type?`\n32: - Prompt: `Run advisor_recommend on four prompts and check which recommendations carry a slash command and whether any result is marked ambiguous.`\n33: - Expected execution process: Run the four commands below from the repository root and read the fields named under Expected.\n34: - Expected signals: `/create:readme` on `sk-doc`, no `command` key on the topic-only deep-loop prompt, `/deep:research` on the same prompt with `in depth` added, and `ambiguous: false` on `/speckit:save`.\n35: - Desired user-visible outcome: The reader learns which command to type for a hub's mode, and is never offered a long deep-loop run they did not ask for.\n36: - Pass/fail: PASS if all four results match the expected signals. FAIL if any command is missing, extra or wrong, or if `/speckit:save` is marked ambiguous.\n37: \n38: ---\n39: \n40: ## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n41: \n42: ### Prompt\n43: \n44: - Prompt: `Run advisor_recommend on four prompts and check which recommendations carry a slash command and whether any result is marked ambiguous.`\n45: \n46: ### Commands\n47: \n48: 1. `bash: mkdir -p /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook`\n49: 2. `bash: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the scripts folder\"}' --format json > /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/nc-011-readme.json`\n50: 3. `bash: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"research loop on incremental indexing approaches\"}' --format json > /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/nc-011-topic.json`\n51: 4. `bash: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"research loop on incremental indexing approaches in depth\"}' --format json > /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/nc-011-depth.json`\n52: 5. `bash: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"/speckit:save\"}' --format json > /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/nc-011-owner.json`\n53: 6. In each file read `status`, `data.ambiguous` and, for each entry in `data.recommendations`, the `skillId`, `score`, `confidence`, `compiledRoute.targets[0].workflowMode` and `command`.\n54: \n55: ### Exact Prompt Table\n56: \n57: | Feature ID | Feature Name | Scenario Objective | Exact Prompt | Exact Command Sequence | Expected Signals | Evidence | Pass/Fail Criteria | Failure Triage |\n58: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n59: | NC-011 | Hub recommendation names its slash command | Confirm the `command` field, the deep-loop effort gate and the same-owner tie rule | `Run advisor_recommend on four prompts and check which recommendations carry a slash command and whether any result is marked ambiguous.` | Commands 1 to 6 above | `/create:readme` on `sk-doc`. No `command` on the topic prompt. `/deep:research` on the depth prompt. `ambiguous: false` on `/speckit:save` | The four JSON files plus the terminal transcript | PASS if all four results match. FAIL otherwise | See Failure Triage |\n60: \n61: ### Expected\n62: \n63: - Every envelope has `status: \"ok\"` and the shell exit code is `0`.\n64: - `nc-011-readme.json`: the first recommendation is `sk-doc`. Its `compiledRoute` has `action: \"route\"`, `selectionKind: \"single\"` and one target with `workflowMode: \"sk-create-readme\"`. It carries `command: \"/create:readme\"`.\n65: - `nc-011-topic.json`: the first recommendation is `system-deep-loop` with a single route to the `research` mode. The recommendation has no `command` key, because the prompt names the topic and asks for no depth.\n66: - `nc-011-depth.json`: the same skill and the same `research` route, now with `command: \"/deep:research\"`. The words `in depth` are on the effort list, so they unlock the command.\n67: - `nc-011-owner.json`: `system-spec-kit` and `command-speckit-save` both rank, with scores less than 0.05 apart. `data.ambiguous` is `false`, because `command-speckit-save` belongs to `system-spec-kit`.\n68: \n69: ### Evidence\n70: \n71: Keep the four JSON files and the terminal transcript. Reduced to one line per recommendation, a passing run reads like this:\n72: \n73: ```text\n74: create a readme for the scripts folder\n75:   status=ok ambiguous=false\n76:   sk-doc score=0.78436 confidence=0.9416 route=route/single/sk-create-readme command=/create:readme\n77: research loop on incremental indexing approaches\n78:   status=ok ambiguous=false\n79:   system-deep-loop score=0.675806 confidence=0.8832 route=route/single/research command=(absent)\n80: research loop on incremental indexing approaches in depth\n81:   status=ok ambiguous=false\n82:   system-deep-loop score=0.65573 confidence=0.8725 route=route/single/research command=/deep:research\n83: /speckit:save\n84:   status=ok ambiguous=false\n85:   system-spec-kit score=0.738163 confidence=0.9168 command=(absent)\n86:   command-speckit-save score=0.7 confidence=0.8962 command=(absent)\n87: ```\n88: \n89: The scores can move after an index rebuild. The commands, the routes and the `ambiguous` value are the checked signals.\n90: \n91: ### Pass / Fail\n92: \n93: - **Pass**: all four results match Expected.\n94: - **Fail**: `sk-doc` has no `command` or a different one, the topic prompt carries a command, the depth prompt does not carry `/deep:research`, or `/speckit:save` returns `ambiguous: true`.\n95: \n96: ### Failure Triage\n97: \n98: 1. `sk-doc` has no `compiledRoute` at all: run `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-guard.cjs`. A `stale-manifest` line for `sk-doc` means the hub serves legacy routing until its manifest is refreshed, and legacy routing names no command.\n99: 2. A route exists but no command: check that the routed mode has a row in `MODE_COMMANDS` in `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, and that the runtime build is current.\n100: 3. The topic prompt carries a deep-loop command: compare the prompt with `DEPTH_WORDING` in `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`.\n101: 4. `/speckit:save` is ambiguous: check that the `command-speckit-save` row in `runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts` has `ownerSkill: 'system-spec-kit'`, then run `runtime/tests/scorer/same-owner-ambiguity.vitest.ts`.\n102: \n103: ---\n104: \n105: ## 4. SOURCE FILES\n106: \n107: | File | Role |\n108: |---|---|\n109: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | Mode-to-command table, the effort word list and the single-mode rule |\n110: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` | Adds `command` beside `compiledRoute` and skips a command whose own row already ranks |\n111: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts` | Keeps a command row and its owner out of the same tie |\n112: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` | Unit tests for the table and the effort gate |\n113: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/same-owner-ambiguity.vitest.ts` | Unit tests for the same-owner tie rule |\n114: | [`advisor-recommend.md`](../../feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md) | Feature catalog entry for `advisor_recommend` |\n115: | [`ambiguity.md`](../../feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/ambiguity.md) | Feature catalog entry for the ambiguity window |\n116: \n117: ---\n118: \n119: ## 5. SOURCE METADATA\n120: \n121: - Group: Native Command Surface\n122: - Playbook ID: NC-011\n123: - Canonical root source: [manual-testing-playbook.md](../manual-testing-playbook.md)\n124: - Feature file path: native-cli-tools/hub-command-attachment.md","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/hub-command-attachment.md, lines 1-124\n1: ---\n2: title: \"NC-011 Hub Recommendation Names Its Slash Command\"\n3: description: \"Manual validation that advisor_recommend adds the routed mode's slash command to a hub recommendation, holds a deep-loop command back until the prompt asks for depth and does not report a command row and its owner as a tie.\"\n4: version: 1.0.0.0\n5: id: NC-011\n6: category: native_cli_tools\n7: stage: routing\n8: ---\n9: \n10: # NC-011 Hub Recommendation Names Its Slash Command\n11: \n12: Prompt: Manual validation that advisor_recommend adds the routed mode's slash command to a hub recommendation, holds a deep-loop command back until the prompt asks for depth and does not report a command row and its owner as a tie.\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n17: \n18: A hub skill such as `sk-doc` used to come back as a bare skill id. The reader then had to work out which slash command runs the mode the hub picked. When a hub's compiled route picks exactly one mode, the recommendation now carries a `command` field with that mode's slash command.\n19: \n20: This scenario checks three rules with four real prompts:\n21: \n22: 1. A plain authoring prompt for `sk-doc` returns `command: \"/create:readme\"`.\n23: 2. A `system-deep-loop` command is attached only when the prompt asks for depth. A prompt that names the topic gets the same route and no command.\n24: 3. A command row and the skill that owns it are one answer, so their near tie does not set `ambiguous`.\n25: \n26: ---\n27: \n28: ## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT\n29: \n30: - Objective: Confirm the `command` field on a single-mode hub route, the deep-loop effort gate and the same-owner tie rule.\n31: - Real user request: `When the advisor picks sk-doc for my README, does it tell me which command to type?`\n32: - Prompt: `Run advisor_recommend on four prompts and check which recommendations carry a slash command and whether any result is marked ambiguous.`\n33: - Expected execution process: Run the four commands below from the repository root and read the fields named under Expected.\n34: - Expected signals: `/create:readme` on `sk-doc`, no `command` key on the topic-only deep-loop prompt, `/deep:research` on the same prompt with `in depth` added, and `ambiguous: false` on `/speckit:save`.\n35: - Desired user-visible outcome: The reader learns which command to type for a hub's mode, and is never offered a long deep-loop run they did not ask for.\n36: - Pass/fail: PASS if all four results match the expected signals. FAIL if any command is missing, extra or wrong, or if `/speckit:save` is marked ambiguous.\n37: \n38: ---\n39: \n40: ## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n41: \n42: ### Prompt\n43: \n44: - Prompt: `Run advisor_recommend on four prompts and check which recommendations carry a slash command and whether any result is marked ambiguous.`\n45: \n46: ### Commands\n47: \n48: 1. `bash: mkdir -p /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook`\n49: 2. `bash: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the scripts folder\"}' --format json > /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/nc-011-readme.json`\n50: 3. `bash: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"research loop on incremental indexing approaches\"}' --format json > /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/nc-011-topic.json`\n51: 4. `bash: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"research loop on incremental indexing approaches in depth\"}' --format json > /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/nc-011-depth.json`\n52: 5. `bash: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"/speckit:save\"}' --format json > /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/nc-011-owner.json`\n53: 6. In each file read `status`, `data.ambiguous` and, for each entry in `data.recommendations`, the `skillId`, `score`, `confidence`, `compiledRoute.targets[0].workflowMode` and `command`.\n54: \n55: ### Exact Prompt Table\n56: \n57: | Feature ID | Feature Name | Scenario Objective | Exact Prompt | Exact Command Sequence | Expected Signals | Evidence | Pass/Fail Criteria | Failure Triage |\n58: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n59: | NC-011 | Hub recommendation names its slash command | Confirm the `command` field, the deep-loop effort gate and the same-owner tie rule | `Run advisor_recommend on four prompts and check which recommendations carry a slash command and whether any result is marked ambiguous.` | Commands 1 to 6 above | `/create:readme` on `sk-doc`. No `command` on the topic prompt. `/deep:research` on the depth prompt. `ambiguous: false` on `/speckit:save` | The four JSON files plus the terminal transcript | PASS if all four results match. FAIL otherwise | See Failure Triage |\n60: \n61: ### Expected\n62: \n63: - Every envelope has `status: \"ok\"` and the shell exit code is `0`.\n64: - `nc-011-readme.json`: the first recommendation is `sk-doc`. Its `compiledRoute` has `action: \"route\"`, `selectionKind: \"single\"` and one target with `workflowMode: \"sk-create-readme\"`. It carries `command: \"/create:readme\"`.\n65: - `nc-011-topic.json`: the first recommendation is `system-deep-loop` with a single route to the `research` mode. The recommendation has no `command` key, because the prompt names the topic and asks for no depth.\n66: - `nc-011-depth.json`: the same skill and the same `research` route, now with `command: \"/deep:research\"`. The words `in depth` are on the effort list, so they unlock the command.\n67: - `nc-011-owner.json`: `system-spec-kit` and `command-speckit-save` both rank, with scores less than 0.05 apart. `data.ambiguous` is `false`, because `command-speckit-save` belongs to `system-spec-kit`.\n68: \n69: ### Evidence\n70: \n71: Keep the four JSON files and the terminal transcript. Reduced to one line per recommendation, a passing run reads like this:\n72: \n73: ```text\n74: create a readme for the scripts folder\n75:   status=ok ambiguous=false\n76:   sk-doc score=0.78436 confidence=0.9416 route=route/single/sk-create-readme command=/create:readme\n77: research loop on incremental indexing approaches\n78:   status=ok ambiguous=false\n79:   system-deep-loop score=0.675806 confidence=0.8832 route=route/single/research command=(absent)\n80: research loop on incremental indexing approaches in depth\n81:   status=ok ambiguous=false\n82:   system-deep-loop score=0.65573 confidence=0.8725 route=route/single/research command=/deep:research\n83: /speckit:save\n84:   status=ok ambiguous=false\n85:   system-spec-kit score=0.738163 confidence=0.9168 command=(absent)\n86:   command-speckit-save score=0.7 confidence=0.8962 command=(absent)\n87: ```\n88: \n89: The scores can move after an index rebuild. The commands, the routes and the `ambiguous` value are the checked signals.\n90: \n91: ### Pass / Fail\n92: \n93: - **Pass**: all four results match Expected.\n94: - **Fail**: `sk-doc` has no `command` or a different one, the topic prompt carries a command, the depth prompt does not carry `/deep:research`, or `/speckit:save` returns `ambiguous: true`.\n95: \n96: ### Failure Triage\n97: \n98: 1. `sk-doc` has no `compiledRoute` at all: run `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-guard.cjs`. A `stale-manifest` line for `sk-doc` means the hub serves legacy routing until its manifest is refreshed, and legacy routing names no command.\n99: 2. A route exists but no command: check that the routed mode has a row in `MODE_COMMANDS` in `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, and that the runtime build is current.\n100: 3. The topic prompt carries a deep-loop command: compare the prompt with `DEPTH_WORDING` in `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`.\n101: 4. `/speckit:save` is ambiguous: check that the `command-speckit-save` row in `runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts` has `ownerSkill: 'system-spec-kit'`, then run `runtime/tests/scorer/same-owner-ambiguity.vitest.ts`.\n102: \n103: ---\n104: \n105: ## 4. SOURCE FILES\n106: \n107: | File | Role |\n108: |---|---|\n109: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | Mode-to-command table, the effort word list and the single-mode rule |\n110: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` | Adds `command` beside `compiledRoute` and skips a command whose own row already ranks |\n111: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts` | Keeps a command row and its owner out of the same tie |\n112: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` | Unit tests for the table and the effort gate |\n113: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/same-owner-ambiguity.vitest.ts` | Unit tests for the same-owner tie rule |\n114: | [`advisor-recommend.md`](../../feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md) | Feature catalog entry for `advisor_recommend` |\n115: | [`ambiguity.md`](../../feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/ambiguity.md) | Feature catalog entry for the ambiguity window |\n116: \n117: ---\n118: \n119: ## 5. SOURCE METADATA\n120: \n121: - Group: Native Command Surface\n122: - Playbook ID: NC-011\n123: - Canonical root source: [manual-testing-playbook.md](../manual-testing-playbook.md)\n124: - Feature file path: native-cli-tools/hub-command-attachment.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/hub-command-attachment.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551309579,"end":1794551309812}}}}
