{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551432271,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","part":{"partID":"prt_1d3995103001VEpUjk65L6xXiL","sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","messageID":"msg_1d399286b001gT56EBwaRlZVuk","type":"tool","id":"call_2214b2263ec3413fa88ee408","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 003\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner`)\n- Session: `fanout-accuracy-runner-1794550137809-1ecgc7`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\n- Dimension: D3 Traceability\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\n- Budget profile: verify (11 review actions)\n- Operator review focus bound as `review_focus`: docs that disagree with code; cross-runtime behaviour; safety of offering a mutating command; holdout hygiene.\n- How this iteration addressed the focus: it checked the operator-facing documentation and the packet's own phase evidence against the runner's real guards and exits, and re-verified every numeric floor the packet claims against the committed baseline artifact.\n- `steer.md`: still absent; no lead rulings to apply.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:63-182`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:25-40,68-69,480-495,1013-1081`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/hub-command-attachment.md:1-124`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:381-405`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:187-230,316-370,413-500,717-790,871`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:15,306,334,357,398`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts:893-900`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:84-149`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/tasks.md:101,139,149-151`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/implementation-summary.md:49`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope.txt:98-145`\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **Runner README describes an unconditional restore and omits the exit code that skips it** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:113` -- The README says a run \"restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths`\", and lists only exit 2 refusals. The code defines a separate exit `3` (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:68-69`), and when a commit or stash appears mid-turn it writes a line with `restored: false, headMoved: true`, returns `EXIT_HEAD_MOVED`, and deliberately does not restore (`:1017-1037`). The guard comment beside it also claims the stop happens \"rather than after the damage\" (`:484-489`), but the commit has already happened by the time the post-turn snapshot sees it. An operator who reads the README as a contract will believe a stopped arm left the worktree as found.\nFinding class: docs-vs-code\nScope proof: `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` and `run-command-behaviour.mjs` are both declared scope files; the finding names one documented behavior and the code path that contradicts it.\nAffected surface hints: `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` §4 and §6 usage text, the operator triage path for a failed arm, `run-command-behaviour.mjs` exit-3 path.\nCase: a measured `/speckit:complete` turn runs `git commit` before the post-turn snapshot; the arm exits 3 and keeps the commit, while the README documents that the checkout was restored to HEAD and lists exit 2 as the only refusal.\n\n2. **The packet's phase map leaves the per-runtime behaviour proof open while marking later phases complete** -- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:120` -- The phase table marks `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/` \"In Progress\" while phases 10-13 are \"Complete\", and the table's own transition rule says each phase must pass validation before the next phase begins (`spec.md:133-134`). The owning phase is genuinely unclosed: its implementation summary says \"Not completed. Planned 2026-11-12\" (`007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/implementation-summary.md:49`) and its closing tasks are unticked, including the one that writes the summary and marks acceptance evidence (`007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/tasks.md:139,149-151`). The cross-runtime claim this review was asked to check (behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh) therefore has no closed packet evidence behind it, only an open phase.\nFinding class: checklist-evidence\nScope proof: the packet is the declared review target; the finding cites the packet's own phase map and the owning phase's task/summary files as read-only evidence and makes no claim about code behavior.\nAffected surface hints: `spec.md` phase map and transition rule, `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/tasks.md` closing checklist, `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/implementation-summary.md`, the parent review's cross-runtime traceability conclusion.\nCase: a reader checks whether the build proved behaviour on all six runtimes, follows `spec.md` to phase 007, and finds its tasks and summary open while the later phases that consume that proof are already Complete.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| `spec_code` | pass (numeric floors) | Packet floors re-derived from the committed baseline: typed combined 44 of 44 (`spec.md:148` vs `attachedMetrics.typed`), plain tune combined 23 of 45 above the 9 floor (`spec.md:149`), false offers 0 of 35 (`spec.md:144`), holdout plain combined 1 of 44 above the 0 floor (`spec.md:144`). |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | The parent packet has no `checklist.md`; the owning phase's closing checklist is open (`007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/tasks.md:139,149-151`), recorded as finding 2. |\n| `playbook_capability` | pass | NC-011 is executable as written: every command is a repo-relative `advisor_recommend` call, and its triage references resolve (`MODE_COMMANDS` `command-attach.ts:15`, `DEPTH_WORDING` `:306`, `command-speckit-save` row `projection.ts:893-900`). |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | `command-meaning-matching.md:44` claims `--real-embedding` refuses `--write`; `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:661` refuses that combination. |\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | The accuracy-runner area has no agent definition of its own; the harness is called by operators and tests, not by an agent. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- Named surfaces: `spec.md` (packet requirements R8/G2/G5 and the numeric floors), `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof` (owning phase evidence), `command-routing-baseline.json` (the artifact the floors are read from), `manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/hub-command-attachment.md` (operator capability case), `runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:381-401` (holdout refusal proven by test), `runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:717-776` (capped rows, policy buckets and loop-without-init proven by test).\n- Cross-runtime evidence status: the runtime table is documented and tested at the argv level, but the end-to-end proof that phase 007 owns is still open, so this review reports cross-runtime behavior as read-verified and packet-unproven.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- `steer.md` still absent; recorded, no ruling to apply.\n- The parent packet owns no checklist, so `checklist_evidence` cannot be marked pass at parent level; treating the absence as a pass would hide finding 2.\n- Phase 007's open tasks require live runs, which this lineage cannot execute under containment; the finding is about missing evidence, not about a missing implementation.\n- The packet's own review packet (`review/`) is excluded from the target per the deep-review boundary; only `spec.md` and the phase children were read as traceability evidence.\n- Holdout prompt text remained unread; the corpus was used through counts and the baseline's aggregate metrics only.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- Every numeric floor the packet claims is present in the committed baseline and meets or exceeds its threshold (typed 44/44, plain tune 23/45, false offers 0/35, holdout 1/44).\n- NC-011's failure triage names real symbols in the current tree, so an operator following the playbook reaches a working diagnosis.\n- `command-meaning-matching.md:44` matches the capture script's `--write`/`--real-embedding` refusal.\n- The transcript scorer's documented safety floor is tested: loop-without-init as unsafe (`command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:776`), capped rows kept out of the start rate (`:729`), policy bucketing from changed paths (`:748`).\n- Backfill holdout refusal is proven by test, not only by code (`command-offer.vitest.ts:381-401`).\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- NC-011 stale triage: ruled out; `MODE_COMMANDS`, `DEPTH_WORDING` and the `command-speckit-save` owner row all exist at the cited locations.\n- Packet floor misstatement: ruled out; all four claimed floors match the committed artifact.\n- README claim that `unsafe` counts a loop without init: ruled out as drift; `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1205` and `README.md:111` agree.\n- Documentation of the arena precondition: `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:36-37` documents the `--source/--dest` invocation, so the missing piece is enforcement (iteration 2), not documentation.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: maintainability\n- Focus area: cost benches and fixtures (`measure-brief-cost.mjs`, `measure-embedder-cost.mjs`, `hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts`, `gate2-golden-prompts.jsonl`, `skill-advisor-regression-cases.jsonl`), legacy fidelity tests, and the duplication cost of the two hand-maintained runtime tables.\n- Reason: correctness, security and traceability have each had a full pass; the remaining dimension is whether the area is safely changeable, especially where two tables or two corpora must stay in sync.\n- Rotation status: D3 traceability complete, D4 maintainability next.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (docs/tests/spec cross-check); blocked (no live execution).\n- Required evidence: bench source and its thresholds, fixture row counts and their consumers, legacy test assertions, and the duplicated runtime/command tables.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/iterations/iteration-003.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/iterations/iteration-003.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 003\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner`)\\n- Session: `fanout-accuracy-runner-1794550137809-1ecgc7`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\\n- Dimension: D3 Traceability\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\\n- Budget profile: verify (11 review actions)\\n- Operator review focus bound as `review_focus`: docs that disagree with code; cross-runtime behaviour; safety of offering a mutating command; holdout hygiene.\\n- How this iteration addressed the focus: it checked the operator-facing documentation and the packet's own phase evidence against the runner's real guards and exits, and re-verified every numeric floor the packet claims against the committed baseline artifact.\\n- `steer.md`: still absent; no lead rulings to apply.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:63-182`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:25-40,68-69,480-495,1013-1081`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/hub-command-attachment.md:1-124`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:381-405`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:187-230,316-370,413-500,717-790,871`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:15,306,334,357,398`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts:893-900`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:84-149`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/tasks.md:101,139,149-151`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/implementation-summary.md:49`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope.txt:98-145`\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **Runner README describes an unconditional restore and omits the exit code that skips it** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:113` -- The README says a run \\\"restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths`\\\", and lists only exit 2 refusals. The code defines a separate exit `3` (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:68-69`), and when a commit or stash appears mid-turn it writes a line with `restored: false, headMoved: true`, returns `EXIT_HEAD_MOVED`, and deliberately does not restore (`:1017-1037`). The guard comment beside it also claims the stop happens \\\"rather than after the damage\\\" (`:484-489`), but the commit has already happened by the time the post-turn snapshot sees it. An operator who reads the README as a contract will believe a stopped arm left the worktree as found.\\nFinding class: docs-vs-code\\nScope proof: `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` and `run-command-behaviour.mjs` are both declared scope files; the finding names one documented behavior and the code path that contradicts it.\\nAffected surface hints: `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` §4 and §6 usage text, the operator triage path for a failed arm, `run-command-behaviour.mjs` exit-3 path.\\nCase: a measured `/speckit:complete` turn runs `git commit` before the post-turn snapshot; the arm exits 3 and keeps the commit, while the README documents that the checkout was restored to HEAD and lists exit 2 as the only refusal.\\n\\n2. **The packet's phase map leaves the per-runtime behaviour proof open while marking later phases complete** -- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:120` -- The phase table marks `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/` \\\"In Progress\\\" while phases 10-13 are \\\"Complete\\\", and the table's own transition rule says each phase must pass validation before the next phase begins (`spec.md:133-134`). The owning phase is genuinely unclosed: its implementation summary says \\\"Not completed. Planned 2026-11-12\\\" (`007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/implementation-summary.md:49`) and its closing tasks are unticked, including the one that writes the summary and marks acceptance evidence (`007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/tasks.md:139,149-151`). The cross-runtime claim this review was asked to check (behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh) therefore has no closed packet evidence behind it, only an open phase.\\nFinding class: checklist-evidence\\nScope proof: the packet is the declared review target; the finding cites the packet's own phase map and the owning phase's task/summary files as read-only evidence and makes no claim about code behavior.\\nAffected surface hints: `spec.md` phase map and transition rule, `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/tasks.md` closing checklist, `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/implementation-summary.md`, the parent review's cross-runtime traceability conclusion.\\nCase: a reader checks whether the build proved behaviour on all six runtimes, follows `spec.md` to phase 007, and finds its tasks and summary open while the later phases that consume that proof are already Complete.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `spec_code` | pass (numeric floors) | Packet floors re-derived from the committed baseline: typed combined 44 of 44 (`spec.md:148` vs `attachedMetrics.typed`), plain tune combined 23 of 45 above the 9 floor (`spec.md:149`), false offers 0 of 35 (`spec.md:144`), holdout plain combined 1 of 44 above the 0 floor (`spec.md:144`). |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | The parent packet has no `checklist.md`; the owning phase's closing checklist is open (`007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/tasks.md:139,149-151`), recorded as finding 2. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | pass | NC-011 is executable as written: every command is a repo-relative `advisor_recommend` call, and its triage references resolve (`MODE_COMMANDS` `command-attach.ts:15`, `DEPTH_WORDING` `:306`, `command-speckit-save` row `projection.ts:893-900`). |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | `command-meaning-matching.md:44` claims `--real-embedding` refuses `--write`; `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:661` refuses that combination. |\\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | The accuracy-runner area has no agent definition of its own; the harness is called by operators and tests, not by an agent. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- Named surfaces: `spec.md` (packet requirements R8/G2/G5 and the numeric floors), `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof` (owning phase evidence), `command-routing-baseline.json` (the artifact the floors are read from), `manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/hub-command-attachment.md` (operator capability case), `runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:381-401` (holdout refusal proven by test), `runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:717-776` (capped rows, policy buckets and loop-without-init proven by test).\\n- Cross-runtime evidence status: the runtime table is documented and tested at the argv level, but the end-to-end proof that phase 007 owns is still open, so this review reports cross-runtime behavior as read-verified and packet-unproven.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- `steer.md` still absent; recorded, no ruling to apply.\\n- The parent packet owns no checklist, so `checklist_evidence` cannot be marked pass at parent level; treating the absence as a pass would hide finding 2.\\n- Phase 007's open tasks require live runs, which this lineage cannot execute under containment; the finding is about missing evidence, not about a missing implementation.\\n- The packet's own review packet (`review/`) is excluded from the target per the deep-review boundary; only `spec.md` and the phase children were read as traceability evidence.\\n- Holdout prompt text remained unread; the corpus was used through counts and the baseline's aggregate metrics only.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- Every numeric floor the packet claims is present in the committed baseline and meets or exceeds its threshold (typed 44/44, plain tune 23/45, false offers 0/35, holdout 1/44).\\n- NC-011's failure triage names real symbols in the current tree, so an operator following the playbook reaches a working diagnosis.\\n- `command-meaning-matching.md:44` matches the capture script's `--write`/`--real-embedding` refusal.\\n- The transcript scorer's documented safety floor is tested: loop-without-init as unsafe (`command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:776`), capped rows kept out of the start rate (`:729`), policy bucketing from changed paths (`:748`).\\n- Backfill holdout refusal is proven by test, not only by code (`command-offer.vitest.ts:381-401`).\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- NC-011 stale triage: ruled out; `MODE_COMMANDS`, `DEPTH_WORDING` and the `command-speckit-save` owner row all exist at the cited locations.\\n- Packet floor misstatement: ruled out; all four claimed floors match the committed artifact.\\n- README claim that `unsafe` counts a loop without init: ruled out as drift; `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1205` and `README.md:111` agree.\\n- Documentation of the arena precondition: `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:36-37` documents the `--source/--dest` invocation, so the missing piece is enforcement (iteration 2), not documentation.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: maintainability\\n- Focus area: cost benches and fixtures (`measure-brief-cost.mjs`, `measure-embedder-cost.mjs`, `hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts`, `gate2-golden-prompts.jsonl`, `skill-advisor-regression-cases.jsonl`), legacy fidelity tests, and the duplication cost of the two hand-maintained runtime tables.\\n- Reason: correctness, security and traceability have each had a full pass; the remaining dimension is whether the area is safely changeable, especially where two tables or two corpora must stay in sync.\\n- Rotation status: D3 traceability complete, D4 maintainability next.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (docs/tests/spec cross-check); blocked (no live execution).\\n- Required evidence: bench source and its thresholds, fixture row counts and their consumers, legacy test assertions, and the duplicated runtime/command tables.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/iterations/iteration-003.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551402756,"end":1794551432271}}}}
