{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551469593,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","part":{"partID":"prt_1d39a4a81001MUMLCtREZb1o7i","sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","messageID":"msg_1d39a39230011Hs20KX7XvOPDh","type":"tool","id":"call_a6d8ac50d0fe41f3b411461d","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Building a per-runtime permission matrix from the six `buildArgv` entries turned \"the arena contains it\" into a checkable claim and exposed which runtimes have no OS-level bound (iteration 2).\n- Comparing the header threat model against `childEnv` caught an overclaim that no single function read would show (iteration 2).\n- Re-deriving every numeric floor in `spec.md` from the committed baseline turned traceability into arithmetic instead of a prose comparison, and all four held (iteration 3).\n- Checking a playbook's failure-triage symbols against the tree proved that chapter executable rather than assuming it (iteration 3).","oldString":"- Building a per-runtime permission matrix from the six `buildArgv` entries turned \"the arena contains it\" into a checkable claim and exposed which runtimes have no OS-level bound (iteration 2).\n- Comparing the header threat model against `childEnv` caught an overclaim that no single function read would show (iteration 2).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -60,8 +60,10 @@\n - Counting corpus splits through `split`/`row_type` tallies instead of prompt text kept the review holdout-safe while still proving composition (iteration 1).\n - Checking every renderer head shape against `BRIEF_PATTERN` eliminated a suspected false-negative instead of reporting it (iteration 1).\n - Building a per-runtime permission matrix from the six `buildArgv` entries turned \"the arena contains it\" into a checkable claim and exposed which runtimes have no OS-level bound (iteration 2).\n - Comparing the header threat model against `childEnv` caught an overclaim that no single function read would show (iteration 2).\n+- Re-deriving every numeric floor in `spec.md` from the committed baseline turned traceability into arithmetic instead of a prose comparison, and all four held (iteration 3).\n+- Checking a playbook's failure-triage symbols against the tree proved that chapter executable rather than assuming it (iteration 3).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n","status":"modified","additions":2,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"- Building a per-runtime permission matrix from the six `buildArgv` entries turned \\\"the arena contains it\\\" into a checkable claim and exposed which runtimes have no OS-level bound (iteration 2).\\n- Comparing the header threat model against `childEnv` caught an overclaim that no single function read would show (iteration 