{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551483699,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","part":{"partID":"prt_1d39a7f02001Gb715lJL5FIda5","sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","messageID":"msg_1d39a5faf001L1xdSlEA7vS56z","type":"tool","id":"call_ed2f34952d0f4befb9ae6930","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: maintainability - Focus area: cost benches and fixtures (`measure-brief-cost.mjs`, `measure-embedder-cost.mjs`, `hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts`, `gate2-golden-prompts.jsonl`, `skill-advisor-regression-cases.jsonl`), legacy fidelity tests, and the duplication cost of the hand-maintained runtime and command tables. - Reason: correctness, security and traceability each had a full pass; the remaining question is whether the area is safely changeable where two tables or two corpora must stay in sync. - Rotation status: D3 traceability complete, D4 maintainability next. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (docs/tests/spec cross-check); blocked (no live execution). - Required evidence: bench source and thresholds, fixture row counts and consumers, legacy test assertions, duplicated table sources.\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->","oldString":"<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: traceability - Focus area: does the packet and the playbook describe what the harness actually does (arena precondition, exit codes 2/3, `offerReached` semantics, holdout splits), and do the tests hold the documented behavior. - Reason: iteration 2 establishes the security posture; the remaining review-focus item with evidence value is whether an operator following the documented path reaches the safe path, especially the arena precondition from finding 2. - Rotation status: D2 security complete, D3 traceability next. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive (runtime table + environment builder); blocked (no live execution evidence). - Required evidence: `man