{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794552044877,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","part":{"partID":"prt_1d3a2ac42002AnstD6Gf4ZGqLN","sessionID":"ses_e2c799a7bffe903YpgFMcmoKDC","messageID":"msg_1d3a29148001jDGWgnFZOo2Y4t","type":"tool","id":"call_d0ad59b4144047fc8760d1cc","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Deep Review Report - accuracy-runner Lineage\n\n- Session: `fanout-accuracy-runner-1794550137809-1ecgc7` (generation 1, lineage mode `new`)\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\n- Review focus: command surfacing in the `accuracy-runner` area — routing-accuracy harness, corpora, transcript scoring, offer recovery, cost benches, fidelity tests, and shared docs that describe them\n- Iterations: 5 of 5 (`maxIterationsReached`)\n- Verdict: **PASS** with advisories (no active P0 or P1; 9 active P2)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\nThe accuracy-runner area was reviewed across all four dimensions in five iterations. The harness is internally consistent on the two properties the review focus named first: holdout prompt text never reaches a scoring, running or backfill path, and a mutating command is only offered through an arena that the runner refuses to leave once a remote, a dirty tree or a moved HEAD appears. Every numeric floor the packet claims was recomputed from the committed baseline and holds (typed 44/44, plain tune 23/45, false offers 0/35, holdout 1/44).\n\nNo P0 was found. Two P1 findings were raised and later re-adjudicated to P2 after new evidence: the project's independent-holdout gate classifies the in-corpus split as a legacy secondary signal, and the runner's network claim is an enumeration the code satisfies. Both P1 records are resolved; their residual defects are carried as active P2 findings so the merge still sees them.\n\nActive findings: 0 P0, 0 P1, 9 P2. `hasAdvisories: true`.\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\nThe verdict is `PASS`, so no remediation plan is required to ship this review. The nine P2 advisories are cheap, local fixes and should be batched:\n\n- Two documentation corrections and one inventory refresh (README).\n- Two measurement-hygiene notes (secondary holdout publication, `offerReached` semantics).\n- Two test/coupling fixes (bench runtime matrix, g2 label grammar).\n- Two hardening notes (arena precondition, credential allow-list).\n\nRecommended follow-on: a single `sk-code` fix pass in this area, then `/create:changelog`. Do not route to `/speckit:plan` unless a P2 is promoted after the phase-007 evidence closes.\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n| Id | Severity | Title | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `iter1-P2-offer-reached-unknown` | P2 | `offerReached` counts an unknown brief state as reached | `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1293` vs `README.md:111` |\n| `iter1-P2-readme-inventory-drift` | P2 | README structure table and code-file count have drifted | `README.md:29,105-114` |\n| `iter2-P2-arena-precondition-unverified` | P2 | Containment inferred from \"no git remote\" with no arena assertion | `run-command-behaviour.mjs:986-992` |\n| `iter3-P2-readme-restore-exit3` | P2 | README promises a restore and omits exit 3 / `head_moved` | `README.md:113` vs `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1017-1037` |\n| `iter3-P2-phase007-open-evidence` | P2 | Phase map leaves the per-runtime proof open while later phases are complete | `spec.md:120,133-134`, `007/tasks.md:139-151` |\n| `iter4-P2-bench-runtime-matrix-incomplete` | P2 | Seven-runtime matrix defines two runtimes; benches fail when enabled | `bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts:26-29,94-96` |\n| `iter4-P2-g2-label-grammar-duplication` | P2 | g2 ids are a second source of truth for scorer labels | `score-command-transcripts.mjs:929` vs `run-command-behaviour.mjs:676-727` |\n| `iter5-P2-holdout-secondary-split-publication` | P2 | In-corpus secondary holdout split published per row and pinned by recapture | `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:537`, `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:91-107` |\n| `iter5-P2-credential-hardening-allowlist` | P2 | Measured turn inherits credentials beyond the GitHub trio | `run-command-behaviour.mjs:768-790` |\n\nResolved during the loop: `iter1-P1-holdout-baseline-publication` and `iter2-P1-credential-reach-bypassed-permissions` (both re-adjudicated to P2 and replaced by the `iter5-*` records above).\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\n1. **Documentation truth (2 items)** — correct the README's restore/exit-3 contract and refresh the structure table and code-file count. One commit, docs only.\n2. **Measurement integrity (2 items)** — either stop publishing per-row outcomes for the in-corpus holdout split or document it explicitly as a published benchmark; rename or re-document `offerReached` so `unknown` is not counted as arrival.\n3. **Test and label coupling (2 items)** — fill the bench matrix for all seven runtimes (or narrow its type) and derive g2 labels from `G2_ROWS` instead of re-parsing ids.\n4. **Hardening (2 items)** — assert the arena precondition with a marker instead of inferring it from an empty remote list; pass an allow-listed environment to measured turns.\n5. **Packet evidence (1 item)** — close phase 007's tasks and summary, or reclassify the phase so the parent map and the transition rule agree.\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- Add to the holdout section: the in-corpus `split: \"holdout\"` rows are a published secondary signal, not the independent holdout; the independent set is `holdout-prompts.jsonl` and is gated by `tests/parity/holdout-independent.vitest.ts`.\n- Add to the behaviour-runner section: a live arm requires an arena checkout; the runner's guard is a proxy, and the arena precondition should be verifiable.\n- Add to the packet: phase 007 owns the cross-runtime proof and must close before the build is described as complete.\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- T1 (docs): fix `README.md:113` (restore + exit 3) and the structure table/count at `:29,105-114`.\n- T2 (metric): decide `offerReached` semantics and align `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1293` with the README, or change the README.\n- T3 (bench): complete `SEVEN_AXIS_MATRIX` for pi/codex/cursor/devin/dsh, or type it against a subset; add a default-CI smoke assertion that the matrix keys match the tuple.\n- T4 (labels): build g2 labels from a shared table exported by `run-command-behaviour.mjs` instead of `STARTED_ROW`.\n- T5 (hardening): write/read an arena marker in `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` and require it in `runTurn`; pass an allow-listed env.\n- T6 (hygiene): split the baseline's `rows` output so holdout keys are aggregate-only, or record the decision to publish them.\n- T7 (packet): close `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof` tasks T020/T046 and its summary, or mark it explicitly deferred with a reason.\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | Four packet floors recomputed from `command-routing-baseline.json`; all met. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | Parent has no checklist; phase 007 closing tasks open (`007/tasks.md:139-151`). |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent owns the accuracy-runner area. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | partial | Six runtime argv tables verified; end-to-end proof open; bench covers two of seven. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pass | `command-meaning-matching.md:44` matches the capture script's `--write` refusal. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pass | NC-011 executable; triage symbols resolve. |\n\nUnresolved gap: the cross-runtime behaviour claim has no closed packet evidence (active P2) and could not be re-proven by execution under lineage containment.\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- Live execution of any arm or bench: forbidden by the lineage write surface, so all behaviour conclusions are source-verified, not observed.\n- `holdout-prompts.jsonl` prompt text: never read, by instruction; the file was inspected through id sets and counts only.\n- Coverage-graph seed: skipped because the seed writer would write outside the lineage; graph coverage mode is `graphless_fallback`.\n- P2 advisories above: none blocks the verdict; batch them in one follow-on fix pass.\n\n## 9. Audit Appendix\n\n- Iteration artifacts: `iterations/iteration-001.md` … `iteration-005.md`; one delta per iteration in `deltas/`.\n- State: every iteration record was handed to the append gateway (`append-mode-event.cjs --mode review`) and accepted with a receipt; the projection was never written directly.\n- Reducer runs: one per iteration (`--create-missing-anchors`), producing the registry, dashboard and strategy.\n- Severity transitions: two P1 → P2 re-adjudications recorded in iteration 4's severity section, resolved and replaced in iteration 5 with explicit evidence.\n- Convergence: no legal convergence; the loop stopped at `maxIterations=5` with `stopReason: maxIterationsReached`. Rolling ratios: 1.00, 1.00, 1.00, 1.00, 0.11; the two-iteration average never fell to the 0.08 stop threshold.\n- Dimension coverage: correctness (1), security (2), traceability (3), maintainability (4), stabilization (5).\n- `steer.md` was absent for the whole run, recorded in every iteration.\n- No file outside the lineage directory was created, modified or deleted; review targets stayed read-only.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Deep Review Report - accuracy-runner Lineage\\n\\n- Session: `fanout-accuracy-runner-1794550137809-1ecgc7` (generation 1, lineage mode `new`)\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\\n- Review focus: command surfacing in the `accuracy-runner` area — routing-accuracy harness, corpora, transcript scoring, offer recovery, cost benches, fidelity tests, and shared docs that describe them\\n- Iterations: 5 of 5 (`maxIterationsReached`)\\n- Verdict: **PASS** with advisories (no active P0 or P1; 9 active P2)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\nThe accuracy-runner area was reviewed across all four dimensions in five iterations. The harness is internally consistent on the two properties the review focus named first: holdout prompt text never reaches a scoring, running or backfill path, and a mutating command is only offered through an arena that the runner refuses to leave once a remote, a dirty tree or a moved HEAD appears. Every numeric floor the packet claims was recomputed from the committed baseline and holds (typed 44/44, plain tune 23/45, false offers 0/35, holdout 1/44).\\n\\nNo P0 was found. Two P1 findings were raised and later re-adjudicated to P2 after new evidence: the project's independent-holdout gate classifies the in-corpus split as a legacy secondary signal, and the runner's network claim is an enumeration the code satisfies. Both P1 records are resolved; their residual defects are carried as active P2 findings so the merge still sees them.\\n\\nActive findings: 0 P0, 0 P1, 9 P2. `hasAdvisories: true`.\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\nThe verdict is `PASS`, so no remediation plan is required to ship this review. The nine P2 advisories are cheap, local fixes and should be batched:\\n\\n- Two documentation corrections and one inventory refresh (README).\\n- Two measurement-hygiene notes (secondary holdout publication, `offerReached` semantics).\\n- Two test/coupling fixes (bench runtime matrix, g2 label grammar).\\n- Two hardening notes (arena precondition, credential allow-list).\\n\\nRecommended follow-on: a single `sk-code` fix pass in this area, then `/create:changelog`. Do not route to `/speckit:plan` unless a P2 is promoted after the phase-007 evidence closes.\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n| Id | Severity | Title | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `iter1-P2-offer-reached-unknown` | P2 | `offerReached` counts an unknown brief state as reached | `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1293` vs `README.md:111` |\\n| `iter1-P2-readme-inventory-drift` | P2 | README structure table and code-file count have drifted | `README.md:29,105-114` |\\n| `iter2-P2-arena-precondition-unverified` | P2 | Containment inferred from \\\"no git remote\\\" with no arena assertion | `run-command-behaviour.mjs:986-992` |\\n| `iter3-P2-readme-restore-exit3` | P2 | README promises a restore and omits exit 3 / `head_moved` | `README.md:113` vs `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1017-1037` |\\n| `iter3-P2-phase007-open-evidence` | P2 | Phase map leaves the per-runtime proof open while later phases are complete | `spec.md:120,133-134`, `007/tasks.md:139-151` |\\n| `iter4-P2-bench-runtime-matrix-incomplete` | P2 | Seven-runtime matrix defines two runtimes; benches fail when enabled | `bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts:26-29,94-96` |\\n| `iter4-P2-g2-label-grammar-duplication` | P2 | g2 ids are a second source of truth for scorer labels | `score-command-transcripts.mjs:929` vs `run-command-behaviour.mjs:676-727` |\\n| `iter5-P2-holdout-secondary-split-publication` | P2 | In-corpus secondary holdout split published per row and pinned by recapture | `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:537`, `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:91-107` |\\n| `iter5-P2-credential-hardening-allowlist` | P2 | Measured turn inherits credentials beyond the GitHub trio | `run-command-behaviour.mjs:768-790` |\\n\\nResolved during the loop: `iter1-P1-holdout-baseline-publication` and `iter2-P1-credential-reach-bypassed-permissions` (both re-adjudicated to P2 and replaced by the `iter5-*` records above).\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\n1. **Documentation truth (2 items)** — correct the README's restore/exit-3 contract and refresh the structure table and code-file count. One commit, docs only.\\n2. **Measurement integrity (2 items)** — either stop publishing per-row outcomes for the in-corpus holdout split or document it explicitly as a published benchmark; rename or re-document `offerReached` so `unknown` is not counted as arrival.\\n3. **Test and label coupling (2 items)** — fill the bench matrix for all seven runtimes (or narrow its type) and derive g2 labels from `G2_ROWS` instead of re-parsing ids.\\n4. **Hardening (2 items)** — assert the arena precondition with a marker instead of inferring it from an empty remote list; pass an allow-listed environment to measured turns.\\n5. **Packet evidence (1 item)** — close phase 007's tasks and summary, or reclassify the phase so the parent map and the transition rule agree.\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- Add to the holdout section: the in-corpus `split: \\\"holdout\\\"` rows are a published secondary signal, not the independent holdout; the independent set is `holdout-prompts.jsonl` and is gated by `tests/parity/holdout-independent.vitest.ts`.\\n- Add to the behaviour-runner section: a live arm requires an arena checkout; the runner's guard is a proxy, and the arena precondition should be verifiable.\\n- Add to the packet: phase 007 owns the cross-runtime proof and must close before the build is described as complete.\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- T1 (docs): fix `README.md:113` (restore + exit 3) and the structure table/count at `:29,105-114`.\\n- T2 (metric): decide `offerReached` semantics and align `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1293` with the README, or change the README.\\n- T3 (bench): complete `SEVEN_AXIS_MATRIX` for pi/codex/cursor/devin/dsh, or type it against a subset; add a default-CI smoke assertion that the matrix keys match the tuple.\\n- T4 (labels): build g2 labels from a shared table exported by `run-command-behaviour.mjs` instead of `STARTED_ROW`.\\n- T5 (hardening): write/read an arena marker in `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` and require it in `runTurn`; pass an allow-listed env.\\n- T6 (hygiene): split the baseline's `rows` output so holdout keys are aggregate-only, or record the decision to publish them.\\n- T7 (packet): close `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof` tasks T020/T046 and its summary, or mark it explicitly deferred with a reason.\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | Four packet floors recomputed from `command-routing-baseline.json`; all met. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | Parent has no checklist; phase 007 closing tasks open (`007/tasks.md:139-151`). |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent owns the accuracy-runner area. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | partial | Six runtime argv tables verified; end-to-end proof open; bench covers two of seven. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pass | `command-meaning-matching.md:44` matches the capture script's `--write` refusal. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pass | NC-011 executable; triage symbols resolve. |\\n\\nUnresolved gap: the cross-runtime behaviour claim has no closed packet evidence (active P2) and could not be re-proven by execution under lineage containment.\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- Live execution of any arm or bench: forbidden by the lineage write surface, so all behaviour conclusions are source-verified, not observed.\\n- `holdout-prompts.jsonl` prompt text: never read, by instruction; the file was inspected through id sets and counts only.\\n- Coverage-graph seed: skipped because the seed writer would write outside the lineage; graph coverage mode is `graphless_fallback`.\\n- P2 advisories above: none blocks the verdict; batch them in one follow-on fix pass.\\n\\n## 9. Audit Appendix\\n\\n- Iteration artifacts: `iterations/iteration-001.md` … `iteration-005.md`; one delta per iteration in `deltas/`.\\n- State: every iteration record was handed to the append gateway (`append-mode-event.cjs --mode review`) and accepted with a receipt; the projection was never written directly.\\n- Reducer runs: one per iteration (`--create-missing-anchors`), producing the registry, dashboard and strategy.\\n- Severity transitions: two P1 → P2 re-adjudications recorded in iteration 4's severity section, resolved and replaced in iteration 5 with explicit evidence.\\n- Convergence: no legal convergence; the loop stopped at `maxIterations=5` with `stopReason: maxIterationsReached`. Rolling ratios: 1.00, 1.00, 1.00, 1.00, 0.11; the two-iteration average never fell to the 0.08 stop threshold.\\n- Dimension coverage: correctness (1), security (2), traceability (3), maintainability (4), stabilization (5).\\n- `steer.md` was absent for the whole run, recorded in every iteration.\\n- No file outside the lineage directory was created, modified or deleted; review targets stayed read-only.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794552015938,"end":1794552044877}}}}
